# DBS programming sessions

Recorded with Wyss DBS Annotator 0.6.0 (https://github.com/neuromodulation/DBSAnnotator).

Each file under `sub-*/ses-*/beh/` is one deep brain
stimulation programming session: one row per stimulation configuration that
was tried, with one `scale_<name>` column per rated scale. What belongs to the
visit (target, leads, IPG, medications and the initial assessment) is the
visit's row in `sub-*/sub-*_sessions.tsv`; the DBS indication is in
`participants.tsv`. Every `.json` sidecar documents its table's columns,
including each scale's name, the contact grammar used by the anode/cathode
cells and the current-split notation used by the amplitude cells.

`_beh.tsv` rather than `_events.tsv` because these files carry no `onset` or
`duration` column and accompany no recording, which is the case the
specification points at `_beh.tsv` for.

Reports generated from this data are under `derivatives/dbs-annotator-reports/`.

## Columns

Programming sessions (`task-programming`): acq_time, is_final, is_starred, program_id, left_stim_freq, left_anode, left_cathode, left_amplitude, left_pulse_width, right_stim_freq, right_anode, right_cathode, right_amplitude, right_pulse_width, notes, with
the scale columns before `notes`.

Visits (`sub-*_sessions.tsv`): session_id, acq_time, target, left_electrode_model, right_electrode_model, left_ipg_model, left_ipg_position, right_ipg_model, right_ipg_position.

Runs (`sub-*_ses-*_scans.tsv`), one row per file with its initial assessment:
filename, acq_time, medications, program_id, left_stim_freq, left_anode, left_cathode, left_amplitude, left_pulse_width, right_stim_freq, right_anode, right_cathode, right_amplitude, right_pulse_width, notes, with the scale columns before `notes`.

Participants: participant_id, dbs_indication.

Notes files from older versions (`task-notes`): acq_time, notes.

## Provenance

No demographics, identifiers or free-text beyond the clinical notes typed
during the visit are recorded. Subject labels are whatever the clinician typed;
check them before sharing.
